      "writtenOn": "2022-11-09T18:56:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In my opinion—yes. This one (on ITelephony) is a version that is intended to switch the HAL into the new mode, it validates the parameter and blocks until the switch is completed. The one on IModule is more like a notification, it must not throw any errors, and it\u0027s not made \u0027oneway\u0027 only because it is recommended not to mix blocking and oneway calls on the same interface.\n\nActually, after I have explained this, I realized I should rename this one to \u0027switchAudioMode\u0027 to emphasize the action. I\u0027ve commented that \u0027IModule.updateAudioMode\u0027 is called after a successful switching. This way, I hope, there should be no misunderstanding.\n\nThanks for raising this question!",
